{
 "name": "Shard Sequencer",
 "isInstrument": false,
 "explanation": "A 16-step granular slice sequencer. Incoming audio is captured into a rolling (or Held) buffer cut into 16 slices across a 1/2/4/8-beat Capture window; a step sequence locked to the DAW playhead (free-running when stopped) fires shards from any slice. Each step sets Slice (or rest), Pitch (\u00b124 st), Reverse, Ratchet (1\u20134 hits) and Gate (25\u2013100%). Global Steps, Division (1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32, 1/8T), Swing, Chance, Jitter, Fade, Tone, Crush, Spread, Duck (dry gate while shards play), Mix and Level. Hold freezes the capture into a locked loop for beat-repeat style glitching.",
 "assembly": "factory/plugins/shard-sequencer/assembly.ts",
 "out": "factory/plugins/shard-sequencer/x.vstai",
